WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.635
[ominous music playing]

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.374
This is really
when the Guadalajara

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.310
cartel came together.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.545
[church bells chiming]

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.814
It was a group of Mexican
drug traffickers saying,

00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:20.186
OK, let's share our resources.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.689
J. JESUS ESQUIVEL:
One of the pioneers

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.724
was Rafael Caro Quintero.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.894
[ominous music continues]

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:35.835
He made what now is called
the Guadalajara Cartel using

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:39.305
the roads of Guadalajara
to send drugs to the United

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.040
States, especially marijuana.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.709
[traffic humming]

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.810
[rooster crowing]

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.347
He came from a small
village in Sinaloa--

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:50.450
street thug, moved
up pretty quickly--

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:54.020
smart, though, for somebody
with a very limited education.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.854
He saw an opportunity.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.457
[music playing]

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:07.801
[speaking spanish]

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.235
[camera shutter clicking]

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:28.087
[speaking spanish]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.557
[music continues]

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:37.697
[speaking spanish]

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.698
[helicopter whirring]

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.968
They pretended to
be sophisticated,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.971
and they were really just thugs.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.874
They ruled by brutality--

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.142
by killing people who disagreed.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.210
[ominous music continues]

